    "description": "Boralex Inc. develops, builds, owns and operates wind, solar, hydroelectric and battery-storage assets across Canada, the United States, France and the United Kingdom. The company reported 3,822 MW of installed capacity and a nearly 8.2 GW development pipeline when its take-private closed on August 14, 2026. Boralex now operates as a private company owned 70% by Brookfield and 30% by La Caisse. Brookfield's interest is held through the Brookfield Infrastructure Fund V acquisition structure and BIF Thunder Holdings Inc., with Brookfield Renewable Partners among the participating partners. La Caisse first acquired 17.3% of Boralex on July 27, 2017, held approximately 15% before the take-private and continued or increased its equity to 30% at closing; no named La Caisse fund is publicly disclosed. A separate 2025 subordinated loan was debt and is not an ownership period. BIF Thunder is an acquisition vehicle rather than a separate PortCo. No later ownership transfer or signed pending sale was identified through August 23, 2026.",
